    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0734" n="722" xml:id="pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Japan)/9–2245</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Director of the Office of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Vincent</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Acheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-09-24">September 24, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>London Embassy’s no. 9838 of September 22 reports a <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >personal</hi> conversation with the Chief of the British Foreign Office
                    Division for Far Eastern Affairs, during which that Foreign Office official said
                    that there were “strong British convictions” that a five-power Control
                    Commission be set up in Tokyo and that therefore no official British reply has
                    been made to the American proposal for a Far Eastern Commission.</p>
                <p>Sir George Sansom, of the British Embassy, called on me this morning and in the
                    course of the conversation I mentioned the matter to him. He said that he
                    understood definitely that the British Foreign Office intended to discuss this
                    whole matter with the Secretary and Mr. Dunn in London and that, therefore,
                    there would be no need to give any particular attention to the personal
                    conversation reported in 9838 unless of course we desired to do so.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J[<hi rendition="#small-caps">ohn</hi>] C[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >arter</hi>] V[<hi rendition="#small-caps">incent</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
